  "verbalization": "The compound in question, (3R,5S,8R,10R,11S)-3-(furan-3-yl)-8-hydroxy-5-methyl-14-oxo-2,13-dioxatetracyclo[10.2.1.01,5.06,11]pentadecane-10-carboxylic acid, is shown to interact with CD276 antigen through a series of targets. It is directly targeted by Caspase-5, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Flavipin, Isotorachrysone-6-O-alpha-D-ribofuranoside, and (+)-Menthol. These compounds all share a common mechanism of action: they act as targets of Caspase-5, which is a protease involved in the regulation of immune and inflammatory responses. The evidence suggests that the compound may exert its effects through a pathway that involves Caspase-5, which in turn modulates CD276 antigen expression. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for the compound in influencing immune signaling, as CD276 is a key receptor in immune cell activation and tumor progression. The relationship is supported by the shared target of Caspase-5 across multiple compounds, reinforcing the likelihood of a functional link between the compound and CD276 antigen.",
